{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide persistent SNMPv2c monitoring from node2 to node1, exposing system identity, uptime, sysLocation \"West Branch\", and sysContact \"ops@branch.test\".","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct queries from node2 returned node1's system description/name, uptime, required contact, and required location both before and after both node restarts. Node1 was also observed active, enabled, and listening after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-01a5d88db3394e11","cmd-d575e0d3e1d24df2","cmd-c0cb07d5a6264537","cmd-2811608b73f548c4"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Configure the branch-readonly community to permit reads but reject writes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The same protected community variable was used to configure and query SNMP. Reads succeeded, two SNMP SET attempts failed with noAccess, and sysLocation remained unchanged. Configuration inspection found one rocommunity and no rwcommunity entry. The literal community value was appropriately masked, so its exact spelling is not directly visible.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c6254a844169433c","cmd-01a5d88db3394e11","cmd-143539bdddd34219","cmd-c0cb07d5a6264537"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the asset register in /srv/legacy2/snmp-readonly-monitoring.","status":"satisfied","summary":"On both nodes, final evidence retained the original 65-byte, mode-644, root-owned asset register with its original timestamp and SHA-256 hash. This matches the preparation baseline.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-87ffce736887439b","cmd-2680d9acc86b4aee","cmd-2811608b73f548c4","cmd-c0cb07d5a6264537"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained Ubuntu 16.04.7 with kernel 4.4.0-210-generic across execution and restart. The installed Net-SNMP 5.7.3 packages came from Xenial repositories, and final package-health checks were clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ac1a1c75385344fa","cmd-ff76a04a727748d6","cmd-2608a660d9ef4439","cmd-c411a6763eed47f8","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.99,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. The successful package installations, configuration replacement and rollback copy, service enable/restart, and node restarts all had direct roles in implementing the task or completing the mandatory restart protocol. The temporary generated configuration was removed, both nodes had clean package state and no failed services, and only normal reboot-created private temporary directories remained. The initial unprivileged apt attempt failed before acquiring the package-manager lock and provides no evidence of a state change; both SNMP SET probes were rejected and left sysLocation unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-292117ffd98641d0","cmd-2608a660d9ef4439","cmd-c411a6763eed47f8","cmd-c6254a844169433c","cmd-01a5d88db3394e11","cmd-9c4d58b054154599","cmd-646cb318cfa1428e","cmd-c0cb07d5a6264537","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. End-to-end SNMP reads and write denial were directly demonstrated before and after bounded restarts. The mandatory restart protocol is complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart states, restart acknowledgements, changed boot identities corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered service, client, asset, and end-to-end monitoring state were captured.","limitations":["The community value was masked in captured output; evidence proves consistent use of the configured protected variable but does not display the literal string \"branch-readonly\".","The fixed after-executor listening-socket observations were empty despite multiple direct executor observations of node1 listening on UDP/161. Successful remote SNMP queries before and after restart independently demonstrate actual reachability.","The retained rollback file /etc/snmp/snmpd.conf.pre-branch-readonly had a clear safety role, but its final presence and contents were not independently inventoried.","No separate cluster-state concept applies to this two-node monitoring topology; restart recovery was assessed through node health, boot identity, packages, assets, service state, and end-to-end SNMP behavior."]}
